3162-## What this skill does
3163-
3164:`spec.k` is a set of K reachability claims. `kprove` attempts to prove each claim by symbolically executing from the LHS and checking it reaches the RHS under the given conditions. When the proof fails, `kprove` exits non-zero and prints a residual configuration — the state it reached but could not close. This skill provides the tools to read that residual and extend `verification.k` until the proof closes.
3165-
3166:Use `writing-spec` before this skill if `spec.k` is not yet written.
3167-
3168----
--
3170-## Why proofs get stuck
3171-
3172:`kprove` closes a claim by rewriting the LHS to the RHS. It gets stuck when:
3173-
3174-- **Symbolic arithmetic does not reduce.** The backend cannot discharge the
